  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224461/assets/3ebe2e4b3436088aa5385757492a8a1f27add8927ea30de71a32a6dc596083cd.png)\n\nThe volume of the cube above is $1\\,000\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.$ What is the length of its sides?",
  "worked_solution": "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{1\\,000}=10\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side is $10\\,\\text{in}.$",
